    "https://www.queens.edu/careers/wp-content/uploads/sites/23/2023/09/everify_spanish.pdf": {
      "title": "Para mayor información sobre E-Verify, favor ponerse",
      "description": "Para mayor información sobre E-Verify, favor ponerse \nen contacto con la oficina del DHS llamando al:\n1-888-464-4218\nEste empleador le proporcionará a la Administración del Seguro \nSocial (SSA), y si es necesario, al Departamento de Seguridad \nNacional (DHS), información obtenida \ndel Formulario I-9 correspondiente a \ncada empleado recién contratado con el \npropósito de confirmar la autorización de \ntrabajo.\nIMPORTANTE: En dado caso que el gobierno \nno pueda confirmar si está usted autorizado \npara trabajar, este empleador está obligado \na proporcionarle las instrucciones por escrito \ny darle la oportunidad a que se ponga en \ncontacto con la oficina del SSA y, o el DHS \nantes de tomar una determinación adversa \nen contra suya, inclusive despedirlo.\nLos empleadores no pueden utilizar E-Verify con el propósito de \nrealizar una preselección de aspirantes a empleo o para hacer \nnuevas verificaciones de los empleados actuales, y no deben \nrestringir o influenciar la selección de los documentos que sean \npresentados para ser utilizados en el Formulario I-9.\nA fin de poder determinar si la \ndocumentación del Formulario I-9 es \nvalida o no, este empleador utiliza la \nherramienta de selección fotográfica de \nE-Verify para comparar la fotografía que \naparece en algunas de las tarjetas de \nresidente y autorizaciones de empleo, con \nlas fotografías oficiales del Servicio de \nInmigración y Ciudadanía de los Estados \nUnidos (USCIS).\nSi usted cree que su empleador ha violado \nsus responsabilidades bajo este programa, \no ha discriminado en contra suya durante el proceso de verificación \ndebido a su lugar de origen o condición de ciudadanía, favor ponerse \nen contacto con la Oficina de Asesoría Especial llamando al 1-800-\n255-7688 (TDD: 1-800-237-2515).\nLa Ley Federal le exige a \ntodos los empleadores  \nque verifiquen la identidad y  \nelegibilidad de empleo  \nde toda persona contratada \npara trabajar en  \nlos Estados Unidos.\nAVISO :\nEste Empleador\nParticipa en E-Verify"
    },
    "https://www.queens.edu/careers/wp-content/uploads/sites/23/2023/09/everify_right_to_work_english.pdf": {
      "title": "– - - -",
      "description": "– - - -\n- - -\n- -\n- -\n-\n-\nIF YOU HAVE THE RIGHT TO WORK, \nDon’t let anyone take it away. \nIf you have a legal right to \nwork in the United States, \nthere are laws to protect \nyou against discrimination \nin the workplace. \nYou should know that \nNo employer can deny you a job or \nfire you because of your national \norigin or citizenship status. \nIn most cases employers cannot \nrequire you to be a U.S. citizen or \npermanent resident or refuse any \nlegally acceptable documents. \nIf any of these things have \nhappened to you, you may \nhave a valid charge of \ndiscrimination that can be \nfiled with the OSC. Contact \nthe OSC for assistance in \nyour own language. \nCall 1 800 255 7688 . TDD \nfor the hearing impaired is \n1 800 237 2515. \nIn the Washington, D.C., \narea, please call \n202 616 5594, TDD \n202 616 5525 \nOr write to: \nThe Office of Special Counsel \nCivil Rights Division \nU.S. Department of Justice \nP.O. Box 27728, \nWashington, DC 20038 7728 \nU.S. Department of Justice \nCivil Rights Division \nOffice of Special Counsel for \nImmigration Related Unfair \nEmployment Practices \n"
    },
    "https://www.queens.edu/careers/wp-content/uploads/sites/23/2023/09/everify_right_to_work_spanish.pdf": {
      "title": "-",
      "description": "-\n–\n-\n- - -\n- - -\n- -\n- -\n-\nSI USTED TIENE DERECHO A TRABAJAR, \nno deje que nadie se lo quite. \nSi tiene derecho a trabajar Debe saber que Si se ha encontrado en Llame al 1 800 255 7688 . Departamento de Justicia \nlegalmente en los Estados cualquiera de estas situa La línea telefónica para De los Estados Unidos, Ningún patrón puede negarle Unidos, existen leyes para ciones, usted podría tener una personas con problemas División de Derechos Civiles trabajo, ni puede despedirlo, debido protegerlo contra la discrim queja válida de discriminación. de audición, es a su país de origen o su condición inación en el trabajo. Comuníquese con OSC para 1 800 237 2515. En Oficina del Consejero Especial de inmigrante. obtener ayuda en español. Washington, D.C., llame al \nEn la mayoría de los casos, los 202 616 5594, o al \npatrones no pueden exigir que usted 202 616 5525 (personas \nsea ciudadano de los Estados Unidos con problemas de audición), o \no residente permanente o negarse a escríba a la Oficina del \naceptar documentos válidos por ley. Consejero Especial, División de \nDerechos Civiles, P.O. Box 27728, \nWashington, DC 20038 7728. \n"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/director-of-alumni-engagement-queens-queens-campus-charlotte-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens",
      "description": "Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens - Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, 28216 Advancement Services Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: University Advancement Department: University Advancement Location: Queens Campus - Charlotte Position Summary Reporting to the Senior Director of Alumni Engagement, the Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens is responsible for planning, implementing, and managing Queens alumni engagement opportunities. The director serves a critical role as ambassador for the University, building strong and sustained relationships with all undergraduate and graduate alumni and engaging them in meaningful ways through communications, experiences, volunteerism and philanthropy. Benefits of Working at Elon Community is foundational to Queens and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Queens should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Queens’ foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Queens. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Queens community. Minimum Required Education and Experience • Requires a bachelor’s degree from a four-year college or university. Experience in higher education preferred. • Seven to ten years professional experience in sales, marketing, communications, events, customer service and/or volunteer management preferred; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Education and Experience Preference will be given to applicants who are alumni of Queens University of Charlotte. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Excellent interpersonal and communication skills (verbal, written, presentation), including exemplary poise, tact and diplomacy when working with a wide range of constituents and diverse audiences. • Proven ability to lead, develop and support team members to achieve delivery of high-quality programs and fundraising initiatives by providing meaningful and motivating coaching, training and feedback. • Strong reasoning skills and the ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, draw valid conclusions, and make well-thought-through recommendations • A desire to grapple with complex systems and to simplify and improve intricate processes. • Preferred experience in project management in similar roles. • Demonstrated competence with technology, with preference given to applicants who are familiar with Slate for Advancement, social media, and other commonly used Advancement platforms. • Demonstrated organization and planning skills (strategic, short- and long-term); strong follow-up and follow-through skills to ensure achievement of strategic plans, goals and objectives. • Strong reasoning skills and the ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, draw valid conclusions, and make well-thought-through recommendations. • Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment and to effectively prioritize assignments to meet given deadlines. Job Duties Foster lasting relationships between the University and its constituents and establish a structured, systematic program of engagement opportunities that will ensure ongoing, meaningful relationships with students, alumni and donors. Hold a portfolio of leadership annual giving prospects. Lead volunteer committees in the planning of milestone and affinity reunion events as well as planning the logistics and programmatic pieces of reunion that all classes attend. Coordinate with volunteers in key cities to support events and local members of the Queens community that support pride and philanthropy for the College. Support giving day activities such as Giving Tuesday and QUnited through identifying alumni advocates, completing their training and providing day of support. Develop relationships through scheduled meetings with key volunteer leaders on the Alumni Association Board. In collaboration with the executive committee, plan annual meetings. Lead the Homecoming committee, comprised of students, alumni and staff in planning the week of activities including but not limited to invitations, programmatic schedule of events and fanfest. Lead the development of alumni affinity programming to extend engagement opportunities for alumni constituents. Community is foundational to Queens and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Queens should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Queens’ foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Queens. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Queens community. Apply now! Similar Jobs Senior Assistant Director, Transfer Admissions Admissions The Senior Assistant Director of Transfer Admissions provides strategic leadership and day-to-day management of transfer student recruitment and admissions for Queens University of Charlotte. Reporting to the Dean of Undergraduate Admissions, this position is responsible for developing and executing a comprehensive transfer enrollment strategy designed to increase transfer inquiries, applications, admitted students, and enrollment.\n\nServing as the primary admissions leader for the transfer student population, the Senior Assistant Director manages the full transfer recruitment lifecycle—from prospect identification and application generation through application evaluation, admission, enrollment, and transition to Queens. The position develops recruitment strategies and transfer pathways that make Queens an accessible and compelling destination for students seeking to complete their undergraduate education.\n\nA significant focus of the role is establishing and strengthening relationships with community colleges, four-year institutions, advisors, faculty, community-based organizations, and other partners that can create sustainable transfer pipelines to Queens. The Senior Assistant Director will work collaboratively across the University to simplify the transfer experience, improve transfer credit transparency, strengthen articulation and pathway agreements, and ensure prospective transfer students receive personalized and timely support throughout the enrollment process. Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens Reporting to the Senior Director of Alumni Engagement, the Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens is responsible for planning, implementing, and managing Queens alumni engagement opportunities. The director serves a critical role as ambassador for the University, building strong and sustained relationships with all undergraduate and graduate alumni and engaging them in meaningful ways through communications, experiences, volunteerism and philanthropy. HVACR Mechanic I - Lead Facilities Management This position provides function field supervision to HVACR trade employees, works independently, and is responsible for the routine and nonroutine care and maintenance of all university-maintained heating, cooling, ventilation, and refrigeration mechanical equipment in accordance with trade practices and in compliance with applicable codes. Possess all skills and competencies of a HVACR Mechanic I and HVACR Mechanic II. Office of Academic Accommodations and Accessibility - Test Proctor The Test Proctor supports the administration of accommodated testing for students registered with the Office of Academic Accommodations and Accessibility at Elon University. This position assists in creating an accessible, secure, and supportive testing environment while maintaining academic integrity and confidentiality. The Test Proctor works closely with AAA professional staff to administer exams in accordance with approved accommodations and testing procedures.\n\nThis position is temporary for the 2026-2027 academic year and will provide testing support at School of Health Sciences/Francis Center. Associate Director of Campus Recreation for Sport Programs Campus Recreation Campus Recreation provides quality recreational and educational experiences designed to positively impact the development of Elon students and contribute to the wellness of the campus community. The associate director is an essential member of the Campus Recreation professional team and provides leadership to one professional staff member, oversees management of sport programs including both club sports and intramurals. Additionally, this individual will be a key leader for a university strategic initiative to launch an elevated club sports program at Elon. Assists the director in department administration and strategic planning. Club Sports Coach-Men's Lacrosse Campus Recreation The Head Coach for Men’s Club Lacrosse is a member of the Campus Recreation staff in the Division of Student Life and serves as the primary coach and leader for the program. Club sports teams at Elon are student organizations, run by student leaders who manage many aspects of organization operations. Club sports programs promote student development, engaging co-curricular experiences, high-level athletic competition, and positive representation of the university. As part of a broader initiative to advance club sports at the university, the Men's Club Lacrosse Head Coach will serve as the team coach, coordinate administrative aspects of program operations, work closely with Admissions to recruit student athletes (in coordination with Admissions), and achieve important fundraising goals (in coordination with University Advancement). This position requires evening and weekend work. Non-Discrimination Statement Elon University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and pregnancy or related conditions), age, disability, genetic information, religion, veteran’s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law (collectively, “Protected Categories”) in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Quick Links Title IX Privacy Policy Emergency Information Our Culture and Diversity Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Elon University . Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Elon Social Media Page Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
    }
  },
